---
import '../styles/footer.css'

/*
 * The colophon: who this is for and what the place is, on every page.
 *
 * It is NOT at the bottom of the document, and that is deliberate. From 1024px
 * up the shell is a fixed-height app frame - `viewport.css` sets
 * `body:has(.site-shell){overflow:hidden}` and `.site-shell{height:100dvh}`,
 * and the content island scrolls inside itself. A footer placed after the page
 * content is therefore below a fold that can never be reached: the body does
 * not scroll. That is how the first one died (a `mt-24` block in Base.astro,
 * 3e1e0ac) and the second (a strapline in the nav rail, dropped when the rail
 * was cut to two links). So this sits inside the shell's flex column as a
 * non-shrinking row, always on screen, and only becomes a scrolled-to footer
 * below 1024px where the page scrolls normally.
 *
 * The line is the one the concept doc names as the footer line, verbatim -
 * see docs/2026-09-10-concept.md, "Positioning".
 *
 * No business model is stated here, and none may be. PRODUCT.md lists bounties,
 * sponsored Challenges, talent and the R&D network as directions where "none is
 * committed and none may appear in UI". "Non-profit" is a business-model claim
 * like any other: it is nowhere in this repo, the concept doc points the other
 * way, and a sponsored Challenge would make it retroactively false. The mission
 * carries the page instead, which is what people actually came to read.
 */
---
<footer class="site-footer">
  <p class="footer-line">For people who believe technology can build a better present and a better future.</p>

  <p class="footer-mission">
    Techno Optimists is a global community of people using technology to understand
    problems, try ideas and build better solutions together. Not startups, not charity,
    not the far future. Fixing an irrigation system this afternoon counts.
  </p>

  <p class="footer-mark">
    <a href="/">TechnoOptimists.org</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    <span>Things can be better. We can build better.</span>
  </p>
</footer>
